{"type":"text","text":"Done. Sheet 4 (level data) is mapped and proven.\n\n## World 1-2 (underground)\nReached deterministically: reset → pause → step 60 (title) → write `$075F=0` (world 1), `$075C=1` (HUD 1‑2), `$0760=2` (area) → step 2 → Start. Live at load: `$074E=2`, `$074F=0`, `$0750=$C0`, `$0770=1`, TIME 400.\n\n- **Layout** — live pointer `$E7/$E8 = $AC37` → **prgRom `0x2C35`, length 163** (`0x2C35..0x2CD7`): 2‑byte area header `48 0F` at `0x2C35`, 2‑byte `[type,x]` object records from `0x2C37`, `$FD` end‑of‑data terminator at `0x2CD7`; the next area starts at `0x2CD8`. (The parser at CPU `$9514` reads `LDA ($E7),Y / CMP #$FD`.)\n- **Enemy data** — live pointer `$E9/$EA = $A0D8` → **prgRom `0x20D8`, length 45** (`0x20D8..0x2104`), ending at the first `$FF` end‑marker.\n\n## Per-level timer table\n**prgRom `0x112D` (`$912D`), 4 bytes `20 04 03 02`**, read at CPU `$9182` during area init: `LDA $912D,Y / STA $07F8` with `Y = $0715` (layout‑header byte 0 bits 6‑7), then `$07F9=0`, `$07FA=1`, so initial TIME = table[Y]×100+1. Entry 1 = 4 (400, used by 1‑1/1‑2), entry 2 = 3 (300), entry 3 = 2 (200); entry 0 is never selected.\n\n## Proofs (each: ledgered one-byte `prgRom` write → reset → re-reach 1-2 → screenshot)\n- Layout `0x2C3C` `00→1F`: first screen loaded rearranged (start ground object moved, Mario left mid‑air) while RAM still showed area type 2.\n- Enemy `0x20D8` `→FF`: Goomba at the right edge gone (`list_sprites` returned only Mario + HUD coin), level otherwise identical.\n- Timer `0x112E` `4→3`: HUD read **TIME 300** (watch: `$07F8..$07FA = 3,0,1→0`), vs 400 unedited.\n\nEach edit was `undo_edit`ed; the two findings were `record_mapping`ed (level `1-2` with both rom_origins, and note `level timer table`) and `promote_mappings` saved them. The throwaway hack `eval-sheet4-b` ledger is now empty, and `use_hack default` is active."}
